# 🖥️ Simulation

The Bumblebee simulator lets you fly a virtual drone with the **same `drone.py` API** as the real one: **Gazebo Harmonic** for the 3D world, **PX4 SITL** (v1.16) for the flight stack, and **ROS 2 Jazzy** in between.

This folder now also carries the simulator **source code**:

- `bumblebee_sim/` — the ROS 2 sim package (launch, worlds, models, python shims, scripts). Ships one Gazebo world: `clover_aruco` — grass field, cable towers, landing pad, ArUco markers.
- `win/` — the Windows installer scripts (`Install-BumblebeeSim.ps1`, `run-sim.bat`, `provision.sh`, …). The big binary bundles (`bumblebee-sim.tar`, `bumblebee_src.tar.gz`) are **not** in git — get them from the download link below.

For the full setup guides:

- 🪟 **Windows** — [Gazebo Setup (Windows)](https://github.com/futureLabKezad/bumblebee-students/wiki/Gazebo‐Setup‐(Windows)) (WSL2, pre-built image, installs in minutes)
- 🍎 **macOS** — [Gazebo Setup (macOS)](https://github.com/futureLabKezad/bumblebee-students/wiki/Bumblebee‐Gazeba‐Setup‐(macOS))

## Quick Start (Windows)

1. [Download the simulator bundle](https://futurelab-uae.technology/s/fz3gBzbM4ENPH59) (~3.7 GB) and unpack it.
2. In PowerShell, inside the unpacked `win-fixed` folder:

```powershell
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File Install-BumblebeeSim.ps1
```

3. Double-click `run-sim.bat` — the Gazebo window opens in ~60 s.
4. Fly:

```powershell
wsl -d BumblebeeSim
```

```bash
sim-run flight.py
```

Dashboard with the drone camera and telemetry: http://localhost:8000/gcs.html
